A FINDING MEASURED ON BOTH ARMS, not what this run was bought for and not touching its branch.
A served turn that ends veto_stall is followed by an idle window in which the loop makes NO model
call, because the armed 600 s wake-up is the only re-entry left. Measured on the control, with the
window boundaries read off serve.log:
  12:26:01.841 turn 1 end (veto_stall, 18 iters) -> 12:36:02.142 turn 2 boot   600.30 s
  12:41:32.763 turn 2 end (veto_stall, 96 iters) -> 12:51:33.054 turn 3 boot   600.29 s
  12:54:24.192 turn 3 end (veto_stall, 53 iters) -> 12:59:26.252 RUN STOP      302.06 s
The third window is NOT a shorter wake-up and must not be read as one: the loop was waiting on a
wake-up due 13:04:24 and the supervisor's duration cap arrived first, logged as
"zakcode.session.framework_stop framework stop requested for agent mind (target mode assistant)".
All 14 wake-up armings in the traces record 600 s; the session's surviving pending_wakeup reads
armed_at 12:59:33.536 / due_at 13:09:33.536 / delay 600 -- the stop turn's own net, never needed.
So of the 2054 s between launch and the run-stop request, 1502.65 s = 73.2% was spent with no model
call. Attempt 3: one such window of 600.16 s, 733 s of 2194 s = 33% idle. The window after the stop
(13:00:24 -> 13:05:46) is TEARDOWN and is deliberately NOT counted as idle.

